      <data key="d12">Argininosuccinate lyase</data>
      <data key="d13">Arginosuccinase</data>
      <data key="d16">Catalyzes the reversible cleavage of L-argininosuccinate to fumarate and L-arginine, an intermediate step reaction in the urea cycle mostly providing for hepatic nitrogen detoxification into excretable urea as well as de novo L-arginine synthesis in nonhepatic tissues. Essential regulator of intracellular and extracellular L-arginine pools.</data>
